      438.29,
      397.2,
      566.39
    ],
    "text": "13. Subject to the provisions of this Act, the bodycorporate shall be able and capable in law, to take and holdany property movable or immovable which may becomevested in it by virtue of any purchase, grant, gift, testamentarydisposition or otherwise, and all such property shall be heldby the body corporate for the purposes of this Act, and subjectto the rules of the body corporate made under section 7, withpower to sell, mortgage, lease, exchange or otherwise disposeof the same.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Bold",
